@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam interface {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}

title The bridge: a ConstraintTheory becomes a BooleanAlgebra the automata reuse

' ── Left→right dataflow: registration → theory → adapter → BooleanAlgebra → consumers ──
component "theories { name = T for [Cat] }\n(TheoryRegistration)" as Reg #DBEAFE
component "ConstraintTheory T\npropagate · label · witness · evaluate" as Theory #DBEAFE
component "TheoryAlgebra<T> { search_bound }\n(the adapter)" as Adapter #DCFCE7
interface "BooleanAlgebra\nis_satisfiable = witness().is_some()" as BA #DCFCE7
component "SymbolicAutomaton · minterms · determinize · lint" as Consumers #CCFBF1

Reg     -right-> Theory   : lowers to
Theory  -right-> Adapter  : wrapped by
Adapter -right-> BA       : impl
BA      -right-> Consumers : reused by

note bottom of Adapter
  `collect_constraints`:
  `And` → `fair_conjoin`,  `Or` → `interleave`,
  `Not` → De Morgan / negation-as-failure;
  then `collect_bounded(search_bound)`.
end note

' ── Formal counterpart (dashed) ──
component "TheoryCombination.v\ncombined_eba_laws" as Formal #E0E7FF
Adapter ..> Formal : formal counterpart

legend right
|= Color |= Role |
|<#DBEAFE> | classical / decidable: registration + `ConstraintTheory` |
|<#DCFCE7> | adapter + the `BooleanAlgebra` it provides |
|<#CCFBF1> | SFA consumers that reuse the algebra (teal) |
|<#E0E7FF> | formal counterpart discharged in Coq (indigo) |
endlegend
@enduml
